    >>> b = jnp.array([3, 4])
    >>> jnp.cross(a, b)
    Array(-2, dtype=int32)

    A 3-dimensional cross product returns a length-3 vector:

    >>> a = jnp.array([1, 2, 3])
    >>> b = jnp.array([4, 5, 6])
    >>> jnp.cross(a, b)
    Array([-3,  6, -3], dtype=int32)

